<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60315" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεατ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gain, win</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δουρὶ δ᾽ ἐμῷ κτεάτισσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.57
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ κτεατίσσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					2.102
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				19.147
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Eumel.
				2
			</span></i>, etc.: —
				Med.
			, <i>get for oneself, acquire</i>, 
				Ep.
			
			fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεατίσσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Man.
					6.677
				</span></i>
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κτεατίσσατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.788
				</span></i>
			: pf.
				Pass.
			 in med. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσ᾽ Ἑκηβόλος ἐκτεάτισται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Merc.</u>
					522
				</span></i>
			: plpf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἃ ἐκτεάτιστο Μίδης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Aet.</u>
					3.1.47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δὲ κτεατίζεται αὐτός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					17.105
				</span></i>
			.</div>
